<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thiaroye massacre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thiaroye massacre took place on 1 December 1944 at the Thiaroye military camp near Dakar, when French troops fired on West African <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirailleurs">tirailleurs</a>, recently released prisoners of war returned from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, who were protesting over unpaid wages and allowances. The official toll was thirty-five dead, but historians believe many more were killed. It became an important symbol of colonial injustice in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thiaroye-massacre.jpg" alt="Thiaroye massacre" width="320" height="158" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Erica Kowal · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thiaroye_Mural_DSCN1029.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
